1
00:00:09,360 --> 00:00:12,817
The upstarts of the great
pirate era have gained a

2
00:00:12,900 --> 00:00:16,317
momentum that not even the world
government is prepared for.

3
00:00:16,400 --> 00:00:18,380
During this exciting age,

4
00:00:18,540 --> 00:00:22,377
there's one man standing at the
epicenter of everyone's attention.

5
00:00:22,460 --> 00:00:23,400
Monkey D.

6
00:00:23,640 --> 00:00:27,057
Luffy and his crew, the Straw Hats.

7
00:00:27,140 --> 00:00:31,500
In order to stay ahead of these
turbulent times, Every four years,

8
00:00:31,720 --> 00:00:35,602
50 global leaders hold a World
Summit in the Holy Land of Marijua.

9
00:00:35,840 --> 00:00:39,640
This event, known as the
Reverie, is about to begin.

10
00:00:44,260 --> 00:00:48,480
The fate of the world is about
to take a dramatic new turn.

11
00:01:03,540 --> 00:01:06,000
This is the current Navy headquarters,

12
00:01:06,500 --> 00:01:11,120
led by the newly promoted fleet
Admiral Sakazuki, new Marine Ford.

13
00:01:11,600 --> 00:01:13,880
Two years ago, in the War of the Best,

14
00:01:14,340 --> 00:01:17,237
Navy forces battled against
the Whitebeard Pirates.

15
00:01:17,320 --> 00:01:19,617
The skirmish ended in the Navy's victory.

16
00:01:19,700 --> 00:01:23,406
However, the destruction to Marine
Ford was quite catastrophic.

17
00:01:24,420 --> 00:01:28,377
The original base functioned as the
heart of the world's justice system.

18
00:01:28,460 --> 00:01:31,460
But in order to acclimate
to the raging pirate era,

19
00:01:31,640 --> 00:01:35,052
the world government constructed
an even greater fortress.

20
00:01:35,960 --> 00:01:39,880
New Marine Ford has become
the new home of justice,

21
00:01:40,200 --> 00:01:43,160
located at the entrance to the new world.

22
00:01:47,300 --> 00:01:50,440
Fuji Dorry dared to show
his face in Marie Joie?

23
00:01:50,740 --> 00:01:52,560
Yes, I'm afraid so, sir.

24
00:01:53,120 --> 00:01:56,337
He was only to step foot in
a base under one condition.

25
00:01:56,420 --> 00:01:59,140
By bringing me the heads
of Straw Hat and Law.

26
00:01:59,640 --> 00:02:03,757
I thought I was extremely clear with
what I told him back in Dressrosa.

27
00:02:03,840 --> 00:02:04,899
What's his excuse?

28
00:02:05,100 --> 00:02:06,680
Wow, scary.

29
00:02:07,040 --> 00:02:09,577
How dare he come back here
like nothing happened?

30
00:02:09,660 --> 00:02:11,260
What a jackass. I'm sorry.

31
00:02:11,560 --> 00:02:14,257
I'm afraid I don't have
any answers for you, sir.

32
00:02:14,340 --> 00:02:16,857
Then tell me why didn't
you boot his ass, huh?

33
00:02:16,940 --> 00:02:21,560
Well, he was armed with theoretical
rhetoric and we were powerless, sir.

34
00:02:22,720 --> 00:02:26,660
If you ask me, it's fair game,
since this isn't military ground.

35
00:02:27,820 --> 00:02:30,120
That yokel is just splitting hairs!

36
00:02:30,460 --> 00:02:32,813
Take him with a grain of salt next time!

37
00:02:38,020 --> 00:02:39,820
It's a tough job, huh?

38
00:02:40,940 --> 00:02:42,020
Fleet Admiral?

39
00:02:43,100 --> 00:02:44,220
Sengoku!

40
00:02:45,360 --> 00:02:48,880
You stay out of this, you
semi-retired has-been!

41
00:02:51,080 --> 00:02:53,860
So tell me, who else do
we have at Marie Joie?

42
00:02:54,280 --> 00:02:55,860
Admiral Ryokugyu, sir!

43
00:02:57,780 --> 00:02:58,610
Ryokugyu, huh?

44
00:02:59,360 --> 00:03:02,080
Then contact him immediately! Yes, sir!

45
00:03:02,900 --> 00:03:05,877
Even though the position of
Navy Headquarters has changed,

46
00:03:05,960 --> 00:03:08,657
new Marine Forge still
serves the same purpose.

47
00:03:08,740 --> 00:03:12,597
guarding the gates of Marie Joie
where the Celestial Dragons reside.

48
00:03:12,680 --> 00:03:15,277
The location of the previous
base where the War of the

49
00:03:15,360 --> 00:03:18,520
Best took place has become
the home of the G1 branch.

50
00:03:18,880 --> 00:03:21,877
The two bases are
situated on either side of

51
00:03:21,960 --> 00:03:24,760
the Red Line to protect
Marijois from attack.

52
00:03:33,060 --> 00:03:34,980
This place is known as Red Port.

53
00:03:35,420 --> 00:03:40,200
Like the Navy bases, each side of the
Red Line also has its own massive harbor.

54
00:03:40,500 --> 00:03:45,265
The government has a novel means of crossing
the war that always draws attention.

55
00:03:45,520 --> 00:03:46,500
Gondola one.

56
00:03:46,880 --> 00:03:47,720
Now depart.

57
00:03:50,080 --> 00:03:51,200
Look, Dad!

58
00:03:51,440 --> 00:03:52,320
It's going up!

59
00:03:53,920 --> 00:03:56,480
Bondolas, bubble-based gondolas,

60
00:03:56,800 --> 00:04:00,153
make their way up to the holy
land of Brichois every day.

61
00:04:03,980 --> 00:04:05,000
They're here!

62
00:04:05,280 --> 00:04:07,633
Just look at all those ships pouring in!

63
00:04:20,140 --> 00:04:21,340
Clear the way!

64
00:04:21,560 --> 00:04:23,325
The royals are coming through!

65
00:04:24,040 --> 00:04:27,040
It's Fear the Sixth of
the Rashwan Kingdom!

66
00:04:27,920 --> 00:04:29,685
And he brought the Patricuses!

67
00:04:30,380 --> 00:04:31,640
How cute!

68
00:04:33,480 --> 00:04:35,820
Queen Moralone of the Tunzim Kingdom!

69
00:04:36,100 --> 00:04:37,218
She's so beautiful!

70
00:04:37,780 --> 00:04:40,900
Here's a toast to all the
lovely eyes in the world.

71
00:04:41,720 --> 00:04:45,120
It's better to die standing
than live on your knees.

72
00:04:45,360 --> 00:04:47,654
King Taco from the Kingdom of the Dead!

73
00:04:47,900 --> 00:04:51,488
Look, King Hamburger of the
Bollywood Kingdom just showed up!

74
00:04:55,540 --> 00:04:58,120
Is there a reason why
he's walking so slow?

75
00:05:03,260 --> 00:05:09,800
Although my pace may be measured,
I vow I will never turn back!

76
00:05:19,840 --> 00:05:21,460
A Navy ship?

77
00:05:32,580 --> 00:05:34,460
Whoa, he made it!

78
00:05:35,020 --> 00:05:37,900
It's the great knight of
the sea, King Neptune!

79
00:05:39,100 --> 00:05:40,060
And look!

80
00:05:40,340 --> 00:05:42,417
The three princes are with him, too!

81
00:05:42,500 --> 00:05:46,100
The Ryukyu Kingdom's finally
here for the reverie! Yeah!

82
00:05:46,200 --> 00:05:47,200
Let's boogaboshi!

83
00:05:47,740 --> 00:05:48,858
Mambo on the water!

84
00:05:49,020 --> 00:05:50,120
Mambo on the land!

85
00:05:50,300 --> 00:05:52,653
I'm bringing the party wherever I stand!

86
00:05:52,860 --> 00:05:55,200
I feel so free! Drum!

87
00:05:55,980 --> 00:05:57,537
Are you two ready for this?

88
00:05:57,620 --> 00:05:58,860
I was born ready!

89
00:06:04,620 --> 00:06:05,450
Damn!

90
00:06:05,600 --> 00:06:07,776
Thought I was gonna drown down there!

91
00:06:09,620 --> 00:06:12,360
Hey, Miss Princess, come on out!

92
00:06:14,040 --> 00:06:15,980
We can do this, Shirahoshi.

93
00:06:16,780 --> 00:06:19,440
Together, let's go to Marie Joie.

94
00:06:22,760 --> 00:06:23,590
Yes!

95
00:06:27,700 --> 00:06:29,120
It's beautiful!

96
00:06:33,160 --> 00:06:35,420
We couldn't wait to see you, Princess!

97
00:06:40,020 --> 00:06:43,057
It has been 200 years
since the Ryugu Kingdom

98
00:06:43,140 --> 00:06:45,497
began its affiliation
with the world government.

99
00:06:45,580 --> 00:06:49,580
But in all that time, they've
attended the reverie only once before.

100
00:06:49,680 --> 00:06:52,280
So this is indeed a rare occasion.

101
00:06:56,980 --> 00:07:01,377
I wouldn't blame you if you had mixed
feelings about our little plan, Koala.

102
00:07:01,460 --> 00:07:02,931
With the fishmen, I mean.

103
00:07:03,020 --> 00:07:04,060
Must be tough.

104
00:07:04,820 --> 00:07:08,520
They make it to the Reverie,
and then we invade it.

105
00:07:08,740 --> 00:07:09,580
It's fine.

106
00:07:09,820 --> 00:07:10,680
And besides,

107
00:07:11,080 --> 00:07:15,497
the Reverie isn't what we have a problem
with, or even the world government.

108
00:07:15,580 --> 00:07:17,617
It's just the Celestial Dragons.

109
00:07:17,700 --> 00:07:18,960
They're our enemy.

110
00:07:23,560 --> 00:07:24,390
Welcome!

111
00:07:24,760 --> 00:07:27,160
We're all so excited to have you here!

112
00:07:43,360 --> 00:07:45,280
She's so big and beautiful.

113
00:07:45,940 --> 00:07:48,160
Hey, just like a dream!

114
00:07:50,000 --> 00:07:53,560
Hey boss, she deserves
a feature story, right?

115
00:07:57,300 --> 00:08:00,260
Princess Shirahoshi Is he gonna be okay?

116
00:08:00,720 --> 00:08:05,360
Forget it, he can't even hear
us We love you, Princess!

117
00:08:07,700 --> 00:08:09,220
Carp, I'm worried.

118
00:08:09,460 --> 00:08:11,600
She seems to be a bit too popular.

119
00:08:12,060 --> 00:08:14,817
Folks have been looking
forward to this for days.

120
00:08:14,900 --> 00:08:19,157
Rumors were spreading saying your daughter
was as beautiful as the Pirate Empress.

121
00:08:19,240 --> 00:08:22,180
She's gonna be a Bone Fight
celebrity, I'm afraid.

122
00:08:23,260 --> 00:08:26,680
She is awfully pretty,
not to mention huge!

123
00:08:27,060 --> 00:08:28,980
So everyone gets a good look!

124
00:08:35,760 --> 00:08:36,737
Um, Mr.

125
00:08:36,820 --> 00:08:38,055
Luffy's grandpa, sir?

126
00:08:38,800 --> 00:08:41,380
That thing over there, what's it called?

127
00:08:41,740 --> 00:08:43,564
Would it happen to be a forest?

128
00:08:44,040 --> 00:08:45,400
No, that's just a tree.

129
00:08:48,580 --> 00:08:51,200
Well, it's the great hero, Garth.

130
00:08:55,140 --> 00:08:58,440
And you must know who
I am, needless to say.

131
00:08:58,980 --> 00:09:00,677
Yeah, you're some stupid brat.

132
00:09:00,760 --> 00:09:01,797
Now out of my way!

133
00:09:01,880 --> 00:09:02,740
What was that?

134
00:09:03,160 --> 00:09:04,620
I must have heard wrong.

135
00:09:04,960 --> 00:09:06,560
He isn't joking, is he?

136
00:09:06,780 --> 00:09:09,015
Unless he isn't isn't joking, that is.

137
00:09:09,100 --> 00:09:10,140
How dare you.

138
00:09:10,520 --> 00:09:14,300
I'm Stella, king of the Goa
kingdom from whence you hail.

139
00:09:14,560 --> 00:09:15,857
You know what that means.

140
00:09:15,940 --> 00:09:18,600
As one of my subjects, you answer to me.

141
00:09:18,920 --> 00:09:23,685
I'll let you off this time, but you would
do well to remember that in the future.

142
00:09:24,400 --> 00:09:28,660
Stella was taken in by Sabo's
parents, who are nobles.

143
00:09:30,820 --> 00:09:32,680
With that as a foothold,

144
00:09:32,920 --> 00:09:34,977
he and his new family
schemed to improve his

145
00:09:35,060 --> 00:09:37,940
standing and wed him to
Princess Isntoinette.

146
00:09:38,900 --> 00:09:43,117
Later, the king and the prince of the
Goa kingdom both mysteriously died.

147
00:09:43,200 --> 00:09:47,377
And as a result, several months
ago, Stella rose to power.

148
00:09:47,460 --> 00:09:50,037
Didn't expect those two to meet up!

149
00:09:50,120 --> 00:09:55,040
Goa is a simple and quiet place, but
it's home to a fair number of outlaws.

150
00:09:55,700 --> 00:09:57,137
Garp's the exception here.

151
00:09:57,220 --> 00:10:00,037
It was home to the leader
of the Revolutionary Army.

152
00:10:00,120 --> 00:10:01,944
They're second-in-command, too.

153
00:10:02,220 --> 00:10:03,400
Roger's son, Ace.

154
00:10:03,620 --> 00:10:04,460
And Straw Hat.

155
00:10:04,640 --> 00:10:07,169
There's something
special about that place.

156
00:10:07,300 --> 00:10:11,480
Now, if you'd like to apologize
by kneeling at my feet, please do.

157
00:10:12,000 --> 00:10:13,000
Piss off, brat.

158
00:10:13,280 --> 00:10:14,640
I got places to be.

159
00:10:16,280 --> 00:10:18,940
The audacity of this man confounds me.

160
00:10:21,900 --> 00:10:24,040
Let me cut to the chase, Garp.

161
00:10:25,320 --> 00:10:27,720
I need connections, my good man.

162
00:10:28,320 --> 00:10:31,337
Hold some strings so I can
become a celestial dragon.

163
00:10:31,420 --> 00:10:33,244
They're all scumbags, you know.

164
00:10:35,920 --> 00:10:36,750
What?

165
00:10:38,040 --> 00:10:39,600
I hope nobody heard that.

166
00:10:39,880 --> 00:10:41,880
I'll be put to death at this rate.

167
00:10:42,000 --> 00:10:42,830
Wait.

168
00:10:42,913 --> 00:10:44,251
Not supposed to say that.

169
00:10:44,340 --> 00:10:45,500
I take it back.

170
00:10:46,720 --> 00:10:47,760
He's terrifying.

171
00:10:55,040 --> 00:10:56,511
There you are, young man.

172
00:10:56,760 --> 00:10:57,819
Are you all right?

173
00:10:58,780 --> 00:11:00,240
That thing can move?

174
00:11:00,440 --> 00:11:02,087
I thought that was a statue.

175
00:11:02,340 --> 00:11:03,440
Is he a giant?

176
00:11:03,740 --> 00:11:07,328
I heard they eat humans and can
melt rocks with their saliva.

177
00:11:09,960 --> 00:11:11,080
No, wait.

178
00:11:11,360 --> 00:11:12,654
What are these things?

179
00:11:14,360 --> 00:11:15,400
Fangs? Scales?

180
00:11:15,800 --> 00:11:17,741
Look at the colors of their skin.

181
00:11:18,060 --> 00:11:19,500
They must be fishmen.

182
00:11:19,740 --> 00:11:21,564
More fish than man for certain.

183
00:11:21,960 --> 00:11:23,842
They are under sea abominations.

184
00:11:24,340 --> 00:11:27,297
Beasts who spread disease
to humans by mere contact.

185
00:11:27,380 --> 00:11:28,900
Don't touch me!

186
00:11:35,620 --> 00:11:38,100
Bandola 2 now deported.

187
00:11:43,860 --> 00:11:44,880
So long.

188
00:11:45,100 --> 00:11:47,420
You folks take it easy. Thank you, Mr.

189
00:11:47,520 --> 00:11:48,755
Luffy's grandpa, sir.

190
00:11:48,940 --> 00:11:50,617
It was fun traveling with you.

191
00:11:50,700 --> 00:11:53,406
I can't wait to see more
of the surface world.

192
00:12:11,520 --> 00:12:12,900
We're so high.

193
00:12:13,520 --> 00:12:14,840
It's like a dream.

194
00:12:19,580 --> 00:12:22,000
Is something the matter, dear daughter?

195
00:12:28,460 --> 00:12:29,680
The sun!

196
00:12:29,980 --> 00:12:31,840
I can hardly believe it!

197
00:12:32,680 --> 00:12:33,820
Look, brothers!

198
00:12:34,120 --> 00:12:37,640
The sun is so radiant I can
feel its warmth! Indeed.

199
00:12:38,940 --> 00:12:41,337
The sky reaches up and up forever!

200
00:12:41,420 --> 00:12:44,900
And the endless sea stretches
out across the horizon,

201
00:12:45,140 --> 00:12:47,980
sparkling in the sunlight
like dancing jewels.

202
00:12:49,180 --> 00:12:52,740
Gotta admit, it makes me wanna mumble!

203
00:12:54,920 --> 00:12:58,780
I never knew that such a beautiful
world was waiting for us.

204
00:12:59,080 --> 00:13:02,021
It's like I'm seeing the
light for the first time.

205
00:13:03,340 --> 00:13:08,040
I must admit, the sun tree on the
ocean floor pales in comparison.

206
00:13:13,840 --> 00:13:16,257
This is where I want to be, Father.

207
00:13:16,340 --> 00:13:20,760
If I can, I wish to stay
here on the surface.

208
00:13:21,700 --> 00:13:24,837
And I want to show this
dazzling world bathed in

209
00:13:24,920 --> 00:13:28,100
light to all the people
of our kingdom as well.

210
00:13:30,520 --> 00:13:34,057
I'll ask them—that's what the
reverie is all about, after all!

211
00:13:34,140 --> 00:13:34,970
all

212
00:13:40,600 --> 00:13:41,430
Got it.

213
00:13:43,300 --> 00:13:47,800
For the record, Sakazuki told
me to find you and kick you out.

214
00:13:50,760 --> 00:13:52,160
Do you want to fight?

215
00:13:54,420 --> 00:13:56,100
Yeah, no thank you.

216
00:13:56,300 --> 00:13:57,829
I think I'll pass on that.

217
00:13:58,440 --> 00:14:02,499
Besides, it's not like you're going
to destroy the conference, right?

218
00:14:02,660 --> 00:14:06,540
Not at all, but there is
something I do want to destroy.

219
00:14:08,280 --> 00:14:09,320
The system.

220
00:14:11,640 --> 00:14:13,760
That aside, thanks for the meal.

221
00:14:14,120 --> 00:14:15,300
It was fine indeed.

222
00:14:15,680 --> 00:14:17,798
You traveled a long way to get here.

223
00:14:17,940 --> 00:14:20,040
How is old man Vegapunk doing?

224
00:14:20,600 --> 00:14:21,430
Well,

225
00:14:21,513 --> 00:14:26,180
not that I could see it, of course, but
he's got quite a creation on his hands.

226
00:14:26,780 --> 00:14:28,360
You wanna give me a clue?

227
00:14:30,860 --> 00:14:34,777
We won't need the seven
warlords, not anymore!

228
00:14:34,860 --> 00:14:38,997
Off your rocker, as usual!

229
00:14:39,080 --> 00:14:40,257
I love it!

230
00:14:40,340 --> 00:14:42,797
I'll say it once more.

231
00:14:42,880 --> 00:14:45,017
The food here is truly excellent.

232
00:14:45,100 --> 00:14:48,037
I noticed you haven't had a single bite.

233
00:14:48,120 --> 00:14:49,417
Am I to assume that?

234
00:14:49,500 --> 00:14:51,265
But you're still on your fast.

235
00:14:52,740 --> 00:14:57,580
If I went, ah, and a fine woman
put some food in, I'd eat.

236
00:14:57,820 --> 00:14:59,137
But that's not happening.

237
00:14:59,220 --> 00:15:02,240
So I haven't eaten a thing
in three years or so.

238
00:15:10,100 --> 00:15:10,930
Help!

239
00:15:11,060 --> 00:15:12,220
Stop the wind!

240
00:15:12,580 --> 00:15:13,780
It's scary!

241
00:15:22,940 --> 00:15:24,420
Simmer down, lad

242
00:15:25,700 --> 00:15:27,520
Did you see that?

243
00:15:27,700 --> 00:15:30,440
I don't know what you're
referring to A giant!

244
00:15:30,700 --> 00:15:36,417
He was in the wall, just staring at us
with some kind of trident and a dumb hat.

245
00:15:36,500 --> 00:15:38,217
You must be hallucinating?

246
00:15:38,300 --> 00:15:40,920
Why would a face be lurking in a mountain?

247
00:15:41,100 --> 00:15:42,460
I know what I saw!

248
00:15:45,200 --> 00:15:47,737
Why are there so many
crows and they're huge?

249
00:15:47,820 --> 00:15:49,960
It's rare to see them up this high.

250
00:15:53,240 --> 00:15:56,240
So these must be birds. How cute.

251
00:15:56,520 --> 00:15:57,880
They really can't fly.

252
00:15:58,280 --> 00:16:01,720
If they peck at the bubble,
they'll fall and die. Go away.

253
00:16:02,440 --> 00:16:03,700
Kaido, come here.

254
00:16:03,920 --> 00:16:05,220
Do your job.

255
00:16:05,500 --> 00:16:06,853
Shoot down these crows.

256
00:16:07,000 --> 00:16:08,820
This is a clear safety hazard.

257
00:16:10,820 --> 00:16:13,460
Don't worry, Kinstein. You'll be fine.

258
00:16:13,980 --> 00:16:15,440
Just you wait and see.

259
00:16:17,480 --> 00:16:22,068
Riding a Bondola, they travel high up
to Marijoire at the top of the Red Line.

260
00:16:24,240 --> 00:16:26,064
I hope you had a pleasant trip.

261
00:16:26,360 --> 00:16:27,713
Please watch your step.

262
00:16:31,560 --> 00:16:32,390
Merfolk!

263
00:16:33,300 --> 00:16:37,637
The atmospheric pressure is different here,
so please use these reinforced bubbles.

264
00:16:37,720 --> 00:16:38,620
Why, thank you!

265
00:16:43,360 --> 00:16:44,300
It's huge!

266
00:16:44,940 --> 00:16:45,840
From here,

267
00:16:46,100 --> 00:16:49,197
the guests ascend along an
extravagant staircase leading

268
00:16:49,280 --> 00:16:51,757
to a land that lies at the
center of all four seas.

269
00:16:51,840 --> 00:16:56,252
It is the largest continent in the
world and rests at the highest altitude.

270
00:17:01,520 --> 00:17:03,760
We're almost there, King Steady!

271
00:17:15,020 --> 00:17:19,220
The descendants of those who created
the world itself reside here.

272
00:17:20,480 --> 00:17:22,860
And the name of this beautiful place,

273
00:17:23,780 --> 00:17:26,300
the Holy Land of Mariejoie.

274
00:17:29,160 --> 00:17:31,400
Oh, I want to live here.

275
00:17:32,200 --> 00:17:33,380
Fruit, please!

276
00:17:34,440 --> 00:17:36,540
It's such a lovely place.

277
00:17:36,780 --> 00:17:39,137
Is that green spot
there a forest, perhaps?

278
00:17:39,220 --> 00:17:40,920
It's man-made, but yes.

279
00:17:41,160 --> 00:17:43,280
So this is it, Mariejoie.

280
00:17:45,880 --> 00:17:49,460
Hmm, looks like it's still
quite a trek to the castle.

281
00:17:50,300 --> 00:17:52,080
Please, come this way.

282
00:17:56,220 --> 00:17:58,867
Take these handles and
hold on, if you would.

283
00:18:06,100 --> 00:18:07,240
An earthquake!

284
00:18:07,740 --> 00:18:09,564
The ground's moving on its own!

285
00:18:10,460 --> 00:18:11,290
Help!

286
00:18:11,373 --> 00:18:12,520
Someone protect me!

287
00:18:13,520 --> 00:18:15,167
This is called a travelator.

288
00:18:15,380 --> 00:18:16,968
The pathway will carry you.

289
00:18:19,460 --> 00:18:22,284
Father, perhaps we should
follow this side path.

290
00:18:22,460 --> 00:18:25,577
Shit Hachi, you wanted to look
at the forest, didn't you?

291
00:18:25,660 --> 00:18:26,490
Fukaboshi.

292
00:18:27,540 --> 00:18:29,481
Isn't the scenery beautiful here?

293
00:18:29,660 --> 00:18:31,484
Better for us to take our time.

294
00:18:31,700 --> 00:18:33,720
I think that's a wonderful idea.

295
00:18:34,000 --> 00:18:36,457
Father, you don't mind if
we stroll for a bit, do you?

296
00:18:36,540 --> 00:18:38,020
It would be my pleasure.

297
00:18:38,460 --> 00:18:40,040
We shall escort you.

298
00:18:40,900 --> 00:18:42,320
Those stupid fish.

299
00:18:42,520 --> 00:18:45,657
Afraid of modern technology,
bunch of savages,

300
00:18:45,740 --> 00:18:48,917
I simply must procure one
of these for my kingdom.

301
00:18:49,000 --> 00:18:50,737
The travelator, you say?

302
00:18:50,820 --> 00:18:53,217
Travelator, actually—call
it what you like!

303
00:18:53,300 --> 00:18:54,130
I

304
00:18:55,880 --> 00:18:59,437
don't know why, but
something feels wrong here?

305
00:18:59,520 --> 00:19:00,350
Not

306
00:19:05,160 --> 00:19:09,837
too fast, not too slow—make it nice and
easy, keep the pace steady, you fools!

307
00:19:09,920 --> 00:19:10,880
you fools

308
00:19:12,580 --> 00:19:15,140
If you stop, then you get the whip!

309
00:19:18,260 --> 00:19:21,460
Someone save me, or at least kill me!

310
00:19:26,320 --> 00:19:28,920
Father, Lock, Lock!

311
00:19:29,240 --> 00:19:30,820
What's wrong, Charlos?

312
00:19:32,340 --> 00:19:36,020
It's a mermaid, and she's big, too!

313
00:19:47,000 --> 00:19:48,120
Open the gate!

314
00:20:02,720 --> 00:20:07,317
It would appear that all the royal families
have brought their bodyguards with them.

315
00:20:07,400 --> 00:20:10,400
They aren't armed, but they
look rather formidable.

316
00:20:11,940 --> 00:20:14,537
They have quite the feast laid out for us.

317
00:20:14,620 --> 00:20:17,797
It'll be nothing but conferences
for seven days starting tomorrow.

318
00:20:17,880 --> 00:20:20,417
So the leaders better
have fun while they can.

319
00:20:20,500 --> 00:20:23,559
Though I suppose the other
guests just get to party.

320
00:20:27,060 --> 00:20:30,097
I'm the king of Samba, and
in my land, Samba's king.

321
00:20:30,180 --> 00:20:32,760
Would you like to dance with me, Samba?

322
00:20:33,120 --> 00:20:34,200
King Samba?

323
00:20:34,420 --> 00:20:36,320
But I can't Mambo!

324
00:20:36,860 --> 00:20:38,137
Samba! Mambo!

325
00:20:38,220 --> 00:20:39,860
Shake it! Shake it!

326
00:20:40,080 --> 00:20:42,677
Seems father is getting
along well with everyone.

327
00:20:42,760 --> 00:20:43,590
That's good.

328
00:20:48,100 --> 00:20:49,840
Can I help you?

329
00:20:51,300 --> 00:20:52,880
So the rumors are true.

330
00:20:53,100 --> 00:20:55,820
You are breathtakingly beautiful, my dear.

331
00:20:56,260 --> 00:20:58,500
Might I introduce you to my son?

332
00:20:58,740 --> 00:21:00,540
He's single, you know. Wow.

333
00:21:00,860 --> 00:21:02,960
She's not bad, Papaw. Not bad.

334
00:21:04,400 --> 00:21:05,230
Princess!

335
00:21:05,313 --> 00:21:08,877
Princess, my handsome son here is a
prince and you might be a good match.

336
00:21:08,960 --> 00:21:11,340
Papa, I like the big lady a lot.

337
00:21:12,780 --> 00:21:17,251
If you're looking for a prince, then
surely you can't do better than my boy.

338
00:21:18,100 --> 00:21:22,159
I have three handsome princes who
would love to have a chat with you.

339
00:21:23,680 --> 00:21:26,300
Princess, which one do you like best?

340
00:21:28,260 --> 00:21:29,090
No one.

341
00:21:32,620 --> 00:21:34,760
I'm sorry, but...

342
00:21:36,080 --> 00:21:38,520
David, you're my type! Why not?

343
00:21:38,800 --> 00:21:40,520
They're princes, aren't they?

344
00:21:41,460 --> 00:21:42,290
Ow!

345
00:21:44,240 --> 00:21:45,160
Damn it!

346
00:21:45,340 --> 00:21:47,500
How dare you humiliate me!

347
00:21:48,460 --> 00:21:52,380
No, she was saying I'm not married
either in an under-Z dialect.

348
00:21:52,680 --> 00:21:54,137
This is all a misunderstanding.

349
00:21:54,220 --> 00:21:56,877
She was merely using
a moral colloquialism.

350
00:21:56,960 --> 00:22:01,717
When this happens, just say something like,
how lovely, but I can't possibly choose.

351
00:22:01,800 --> 00:22:03,741
Gotta let them down softly, okay?

352
00:22:04,600 --> 00:22:07,365
But if I told them that,
then I would be lying.

353
00:22:07,540 --> 00:22:09,580
It's not lying, it's redirecting.

354
00:22:09,840 --> 00:22:12,077
Better than starting a
diplomatic emergency.

355
00:22:12,160 --> 00:22:13,160
Now let's go.

356
00:22:13,680 --> 00:22:14,621
So let's eat it.

357
00:22:18,180 --> 00:22:19,140
How cute.

358
00:22:20,800 --> 00:22:22,388
You're like a little fairy.

359
00:22:22,620 --> 00:22:24,040
I could just eat you up.

360
00:22:24,400 --> 00:22:26,317
I'm a warrior, I'll have you know.

361
00:22:26,400 --> 00:22:28,047
so that is not a compliment!

362
00:22:29,000 --> 00:22:30,960
You okay there, Leo?

363
00:22:31,260 --> 00:22:33,100
I didn't mean anything by it.

364
00:22:33,260 --> 00:22:35,000
Sorry I insulted you. Huh?

365
00:22:35,980 --> 00:22:37,480
Well, then that's okay.

366
00:22:38,000 --> 00:22:38,880
He's safe.

367
00:22:39,120 --> 00:22:40,680
She is nice, after all.

368
00:22:40,780 --> 00:22:42,440
You certainly can move fast.

369
00:22:42,780 --> 00:22:45,486
I didn't notice at all
until Karoo spotted you.

370
00:22:45,600 --> 00:22:50,037
I allowed myself to be seen because I heard
that you were friends with Luffy Land.

371
00:22:50,120 --> 00:22:52,708
We are the Straw Hat
subordinates, you know.

372
00:22:52,940 --> 00:22:54,620
And we're pirates, too.

373
00:22:55,040 --> 00:22:56,020
Little pirates?

374
00:22:57,100 --> 00:22:58,440
That's so cute!

375
00:22:58,720 --> 00:23:00,397
And it's a pleasure to meet you.

376
00:23:00,480 --> 00:23:02,304
A pleasure to meet you as well!

377
00:23:02,540 --> 00:23:04,246
This is such a nice surprise.

378
00:23:04,500 --> 00:23:08,500
I wasn't expecting to meet so many
of Lucy's friends at the reverie.

379
00:23:08,820 --> 00:23:12,702
But then again, the Straw Hats are
traveling the world, I suppose.

380
00:23:12,860 --> 00:23:14,877
Did Lucy visit your country as well?

381
00:23:14,960 --> 00:23:16,760
Or Luffy, I mean?

382
00:23:17,940 --> 00:23:18,770
Yeah!

383
00:23:18,853 --> 00:23:19,683
Tell us!

384
00:23:19,860 --> 00:23:20,700
He did.

385
00:23:21,140 --> 00:23:27,160
In fact, if it wasn't for them, The kingdom
of Alabasta wouldn't even exist today.

386
00:23:27,960 --> 00:23:32,380
Princess Vivi from Alabasta, a desert
kingdom located on the Grand Line.

387
00:23:32,620 --> 00:23:35,317
She encountered the Straw
Hats more than two years ago

388
00:23:35,400 --> 00:23:38,753
and traveled on the ship as
a close friend for some time.

389
00:23:40,220 --> 00:23:43,017
Crocodile, who was a warlord
of the sea at the time,

390
00:23:43,100 --> 00:23:45,177
looked to take control of Alabasta.

391
00:23:45,260 --> 00:23:46,090
As a result,

392
00:23:46,173 --> 00:23:50,351
the kingdom was locked in civil war
between the royal army and rebel forces.

393
00:23:50,620 --> 00:23:53,620
Crocodile's plot was thwarted
by Luffy and friends.

394
00:23:53,780 --> 00:23:57,020
At last, the Alabasta
Kingdom was saved. However,

395
00:23:57,440 --> 00:23:59,677
the world government reported the Navy was

396
00:23:59,760 --> 00:24:02,936
responsible to hide the fact
that pirates won the day.

397
00:24:04,220 --> 00:24:06,396
They don't like to be seen as heroes.

398
00:24:07,560 --> 00:24:10,197
Their bounties keep
getting higher and higher.

399
00:24:10,280 --> 00:24:12,617
The whole world probably
knows about them now.

400
00:24:12,700 --> 00:24:15,740
Still, they haven't changed
one bit, my friends.

401
00:24:16,220 --> 00:24:18,797
When I read about what
happened in Dressrosa, I knew.

402
00:24:18,880 --> 00:24:20,720
They saw someone in need,

403
00:24:21,080 --> 00:24:25,021
so I'll bet they did everything in
their power to save them, right?

404
00:24:25,400 --> 00:24:26,740
Yeah, he did!

405
00:24:28,820 --> 00:24:30,880
Luffy did more than just save me.

406
00:24:31,200 --> 00:24:32,435
He saved our kingdom.

407
00:24:32,800 --> 00:24:35,640
The Straw Hats are the
heroes of all Dressrosa!

408
00:24:40,000 --> 00:24:42,080
I miss you, Lucy.

409
00:24:44,500 --> 00:24:45,480
Excuse me?

410
00:24:47,180 --> 00:24:49,517
Um, were the two of you talking about Mr.

411
00:24:49,600 --> 00:24:50,560
Luffy just now?

412
00:24:51,580 --> 00:24:53,040
The Mermaid Princess!

413
00:24:54,200 --> 00:24:55,030
Shirahoshi!

414
00:24:56,140 --> 00:24:58,577
Talking about him doesn't
mean they know him.

415
00:24:58,660 --> 00:25:00,417
Luffy's still a pirate, after all.

416
00:25:00,500 --> 00:25:03,147
You mustn't let people
know he's your friend.

417
00:25:04,220 --> 00:25:07,020
Hmm, the Mermaid Princess knows Luffy?

418
00:25:07,320 --> 00:25:10,097
Wait, you were asking if
we're friends with Luffy?

419
00:25:10,180 --> 00:25:11,180
Hold on, Rebecca.

420
00:25:11,380 --> 00:25:12,917
You shouldn't say too much.

421
00:25:13,000 --> 00:25:14,477
Yes, I was right!

422
00:25:14,560 --> 00:25:17,460
So you were talking about him! Stop it!

423
00:25:17,620 --> 00:25:19,577
Maybe they were saying how bad he is!

424
00:25:19,660 --> 00:25:22,700
I owe a great debt of gratitude to Luffy.

425
00:25:25,960 --> 00:25:26,920
Us too!

426
00:25:49,020 --> 00:25:53,060
Oh, speaking of Luffy, he
sure eats a lot, doesn't he?

427
00:25:53,340 --> 00:25:56,752
Yeah, if he's not eating, he's
probably thinking about it.

428
00:25:57,440 --> 00:26:00,057
He certainly enjoys a
good feast, doesn't he?

429
00:26:00,140 --> 00:26:01,880
Seems they're having fun.

430
00:26:02,260 --> 00:26:03,140
That they are.

431
00:26:03,320 --> 00:26:06,517
I would say this bodes well
for the future of our nations.

432
00:26:06,600 --> 00:26:09,071
We've made good friends in no time at all.

433
00:26:09,180 --> 00:26:11,651
Though I admit, it's a strange connection.

434
00:26:12,280 --> 00:26:16,260
Indeed, royal families united by
the goodwill of the Straw Hats.

435
00:26:18,180 --> 00:26:21,160
Excuse me, aren't you
Rebecca from Dressrosa?

436
00:26:22,540 --> 00:26:24,320
Wow, look who it is!

437
00:26:25,100 --> 00:26:26,200
It's me, Sai!

438
00:26:26,860 --> 00:26:30,978
Funny, feels like the last time I
ran into you was just the other day!

439
00:26:31,220 --> 00:26:32,177
And have you been well?

440
00:26:32,260 --> 00:26:33,260
Better than ever!

441
00:26:33,760 --> 00:26:36,420
It seems he is from Kano's Hapasue army.

442
00:26:36,760 --> 00:26:40,857
I heard that the old warrior Qin
Zhao stepped down not too long ago.

443
00:26:40,940 --> 00:26:41,880
He did.

444
00:26:42,120 --> 00:26:43,649
That man's the new leader.

445
00:26:44,120 --> 00:26:45,120
Hi, Aisa!

446
00:26:45,900 --> 00:26:47,060
Hey, brother!

447
00:26:47,380 --> 00:26:49,860
I didn't think I'd see you here, too, Leo.

448
00:26:50,200 --> 00:26:51,900
I'm the secret bodyguard.

449
00:26:53,000 --> 00:26:55,780
What a reliable ally. Agreed.

450
00:26:56,460 --> 00:26:57,872
Is he a friend of yours?

451
00:26:58,240 --> 00:27:01,652
Yeah, and we exchanged cups
of sake with Lufilun together.

452
00:27:02,520 --> 00:27:03,560
Hey, Leo.

453
00:27:03,780 --> 00:27:07,337
Listen, I'm doing my part in working
hard for the kingdom of Kano.

454
00:27:07,420 --> 00:27:10,317
But after this bodyguard job
is done, I'm cutting ties.

455
00:27:10,400 --> 00:27:13,297
When I make a vow, I
don't take it lightly.

456
00:27:13,380 --> 00:27:16,577
I owe a great debt to the Straw Hats.

457
00:27:16,660 --> 00:27:17,537
After they saved me,

458
00:27:17,620 --> 00:27:21,237
and I intend to pay it back all seven

459
00:27:21,320 --> 00:27:24,077
representatives of the
Straw Hat fleet along with

460
00:27:24,160 --> 00:27:29,277
all five thousand six hundred of our troops
have to be ready to aid him at any time!

461
00:27:29,360 --> 00:27:34,760
Hmm, I heard the other members
have started preparing as well?

462
00:27:42,400 --> 00:27:43,700
What is this?

463
00:27:43,980 --> 00:27:46,897
You think you can resign
from the Standing Kingdom?

464
00:27:46,980 --> 00:27:47,862
Just like that!

465
00:27:48,120 --> 00:27:49,180
Tell me why!

466
00:27:49,800 --> 00:27:52,480
Forgive me, but there's
a debt I must repay.

467
00:27:54,140 --> 00:27:54,970
Barrier!

468
00:27:55,053 --> 00:27:55,960
Barrier crush!

469
00:27:58,660 --> 00:28:02,360
Stay behind the barrier and
cross your fingers for good luck.

470
00:28:02,720 --> 00:28:05,057
That's my battle-tested
secret for success.

471
00:28:05,140 --> 00:28:06,220
We surrender!

472
00:28:06,680 --> 00:28:08,460
Please, just show us mercy.

473
00:28:08,680 --> 00:28:10,177
We'll even serve under you.

474
00:28:10,260 --> 00:28:11,319
Whatever you want.

475
00:28:12,520 --> 00:28:13,350
Good.

476
00:28:14,100 --> 00:28:15,660
Then put this on.

477
00:28:16,360 --> 00:28:17,740
What is it?

478
00:28:19,340 --> 00:28:24,440
Wear this and show your support
for the Straw Hats with us. Do it!

479
00:28:28,440 --> 00:28:31,820
Two unidentified ships
are approaching, sir.

480
00:28:32,120 --> 00:28:33,840
Here to avenge Doflamingo.

481
00:28:35,760 --> 00:28:36,880
What Cavendish?

482
00:28:37,080 --> 00:28:38,668
Oh, it's nothing like that.

483
00:28:39,600 --> 00:28:43,580
I was the prince of the bourgeois
kingdom, as you may already know.

484
00:28:49,340 --> 00:28:53,516
Naturally, all the women in the
kingdom were absolutely crazy about me.

485
00:28:53,820 --> 00:28:56,680
They refused to marry any
man other than myself,

486
00:28:56,920 --> 00:29:02,100
and so I was expelled from the kingdom,
charged with the crime of being too popular.

487
00:29:03,280 --> 00:29:08,480
Uh, so in other words, the ships pursuing
us are not enemies, but my adoring fans.

488
00:29:12,580 --> 00:29:16,227
I know there's people even
stronger than Doflamingo out there,

489
00:29:16,380 --> 00:29:19,737
and I'm sure that Straw Hat will
face many of them in combat.

490
00:29:19,820 --> 00:29:24,000
If we want to help, we must build
our own strength, too. Agreed.

491
00:29:24,300 --> 00:29:26,577
My crew and I are training hard every day,

492
00:29:26,660 --> 00:29:31,057
and I hope we can fight
together by Luffy Lund's side.

493
00:29:31,140 --> 00:29:32,040
Right!

494
00:29:37,380 --> 00:29:39,840
Well, if it isn't Princess Phoebe!

495
00:29:41,660 --> 00:29:42,490
Wapol!

496
00:29:44,580 --> 00:29:45,780
You fool!

497
00:29:49,140 --> 00:29:51,460
What's a goon like you doing here?

498
00:29:53,060 --> 00:29:54,780
A fine question.

499
00:29:55,020 --> 00:29:57,437
I have Straw Hat to thank.

500
00:29:57,520 --> 00:30:02,600
He sent me flying away to a strange
and distant land, but I'm back, baby!

501
00:30:02,820 --> 00:30:03,960
And in charge!

502
00:30:04,300 --> 00:30:05,240
So, you fools.

503
00:30:05,480 --> 00:30:08,157
Want to know how my darling
rose to power again?

504
00:30:08,240 --> 00:30:09,358
What a coincidence!

505
00:30:09,580 --> 00:30:12,660
They must be friends of
Luffy's as well! Not quite.

506
00:30:12,960 --> 00:30:14,080
He's an enemy.

507
00:30:16,380 --> 00:30:19,160
That old funny Daddy
King Cobra doing well?

508
00:30:19,560 --> 00:30:22,360
Actually, I know he's not doing well.

509
00:30:22,540 --> 00:30:23,700
I saw him earlier.

510
00:30:23,900 --> 00:30:26,018
I was making a joke at your expense.

511
00:30:27,520 --> 00:30:29,560
You, darling, you're the best!

512
00:30:29,840 --> 00:30:31,680
I rarely call Dick your hero!

513
00:30:32,020 --> 00:30:34,373
You're the funniest man in the universe!

514
00:30:34,600 --> 00:30:35,800
Gush, gush, gush!

515
00:30:39,180 --> 00:30:40,010
Huh?

516
00:30:40,093 --> 00:30:41,487
That's enough of your jokes.

517
00:30:42,200 --> 00:30:44,788
It's sickening that you
came to power again.

518
00:30:44,960 --> 00:30:47,900
I feel sorry for whatever
country you rule.

519
00:30:48,680 --> 00:30:49,640
Yee-hee-hee!

520
00:30:49,820 --> 00:30:52,340
The world government should be ashamed.

521
00:30:52,580 --> 00:30:55,462
They've got no standards
if they let you back in.

522
00:30:56,340 --> 00:30:57,170
Dalton!

523
00:30:57,253 --> 00:30:58,240
And that witch!

524
00:30:58,600 --> 00:31:00,340
How are you still alive?

525
00:31:00,520 --> 00:31:02,420
Asking about my beauty regimen?

526
00:31:02,640 --> 00:31:03,780
Not a chance!

527
00:31:04,320 --> 00:31:05,920
Dalton! Dr. Kureha!

528
00:31:06,140 --> 00:31:07,611
So nice to see you again!

529
00:31:07,860 --> 00:31:08,960
Hello, Vivi.

530
00:31:09,200 --> 00:31:11,318
You're looking more regal than ever.

531
00:31:12,540 --> 00:31:13,600
Are you happy?

532
00:31:14,000 --> 00:31:18,757
If I'd known you were a princess back then,
I would have stuck you in a higher bill.

533
00:31:18,840 --> 00:31:20,160
That's for darn sure.

534
00:31:20,560 --> 00:31:21,880
Who are these two?

535
00:31:22,240 --> 00:31:24,337
They're friends from a
snow-covered island that

536
00:31:24,420 --> 00:31:27,361
I traveled to with Luffy
and the other Straw Hats.

537
00:31:29,860 --> 00:31:34,000
While we were on our way to
Alabasta, Nami suddenly fell ill.

538
00:31:34,340 --> 00:31:35,797
We needed to find a doctor.

539
00:31:35,880 --> 00:31:38,586
So we stopped on the
nearest inhabited island.

540
00:31:42,360 --> 00:31:47,007
Dalton helped Luffy get rid of Wapol and
became a bit of a hero to the kingdom.

541
00:31:47,580 --> 00:31:49,420
So he was appointed as king,

542
00:31:49,640 --> 00:31:53,157
and the Drum Kingdom was reborn
as the Cherry Blossom Kingdom.

543
00:31:53,240 --> 00:31:54,440
That's lovely.

544
00:31:55,980 --> 00:31:57,400
Hey, hey, hey!

545
00:31:57,840 --> 00:31:59,820
You're getting a real big head.

546
00:32:00,100 --> 00:32:03,800
Perhaps I need to remind you,
you're still my subordinate.

547
00:32:04,360 --> 00:32:06,480
Those days have long since passed.

548
00:32:07,180 --> 00:32:08,010
Now.

549
00:32:12,920 --> 00:32:14,257
I've become a king.

550
00:32:14,340 --> 00:32:16,160
I won't bow to you.

551
00:32:18,400 --> 00:32:19,580
Wow, Dalton.

552
00:32:19,760 --> 00:32:21,477
You're acting like royalty already.

553
00:32:21,560 --> 00:32:22,880
You are a natural.

554
00:32:23,460 --> 00:32:24,290
Uh, come on.

555
00:32:25,540 --> 00:32:26,370
Nah!

556
00:32:26,453 --> 00:32:27,283
Listen up, Dalton!

557
00:32:27,366 --> 00:32:29,060
You useless goody-two-shoes!

558
00:32:29,180 --> 00:32:32,945
If you wanna make it as a ruler,
you gotta get your hands dirty!

559
00:32:33,360 --> 00:32:35,420
I clawed my way back to the top,

560
00:32:35,580 --> 00:32:39,377
making a fortune with my munch-munch
powers, and trust me, I know!

561
00:32:39,460 --> 00:32:42,300
The higher up you climb,
the sooner you'll see!

562
00:32:42,460 --> 00:32:43,857
This whole world is corrupt!

563
00:32:43,940 --> 00:32:47,637
That tip was free, but the next
one will cost you your life!

564
00:32:47,720 --> 00:32:50,477
Oh, and by the way, did you
read the article on Luffy?

565
00:32:50,560 --> 00:32:52,300
Yes, from top to bottom.

566
00:32:52,880 --> 00:32:54,040
Oh, I get it.

567
00:32:54,260 --> 00:32:55,920
You're like us. Huh?

568
00:32:56,720 --> 00:32:58,020
Lucy's fan.

569
00:32:58,480 --> 00:33:00,892
Be honest, you like Luffy Lynn, don't ya?

570
00:33:04,580 --> 00:33:05,840
He's the best.

571
00:33:06,760 --> 00:33:08,140
I thought so.

572
00:33:10,200 --> 00:33:13,680
The underwater prison, impel down.

573
00:33:20,460 --> 00:33:24,117
The bottom floor level six holds the most

574
00:33:24,200 --> 00:33:26,137
dangerous criminals the
world has ever known.

575
00:33:26,220 --> 00:33:30,000
It's called the infinite hell.

576
00:33:35,840 --> 00:33:38,697
Putting me in solitary, are you?

577
00:33:38,780 --> 00:33:42,157
I'm so lonely, why Magellan?

578
00:33:42,240 --> 00:33:46,957
Or is this a plot to protect me? Maybe?

579
00:33:47,040 --> 00:33:53,297
Is there an assassin from
on high out to kill me?

580
00:33:53,380 --> 00:33:56,477
Of course I'd better
watch my loose tongue.

581
00:33:56,560 --> 00:33:58,937
What a rotten mess I could cause!

582
00:33:59,020 --> 00:34:03,517
Just think—what if I told the whole
world the secret Maurice was hiding? Why?

583
00:34:03,600 --> 00:34:09,457
why Why does it matter

584
00:34:09,540 --> 00:34:10,775
if it's revealed now?

585
00:34:11,220 --> 00:34:13,040
Power doesn't last long.

586
00:34:13,400 --> 00:34:16,180
It'll rot faster than anyone thinks.

587
00:34:42,020 --> 00:34:42,850
I don't know.
